.TH ZARK-GNOME-APP 1 "" "zark-gnome-app 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zark-gnome-app \- GNOME app showing the state of zark backups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zark-gnome-app
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zark-gnome-app
opens a window with the state of the backups zark makes: how full the
system pools are, each backup drive with its last backup, its space and its
backup points by month, the datasets left out of backups, and a backup
running in a terminal, with its progress.
.PP
It reads zark's status files,
.I /run/zark/progress.json
and
.IR /var/lib/zark/status.json ,
through the reader of the installed zark in
.IR /usr/share/zark ,
and the output of
.BR zpool (8)
.BR list ,
.BR zfs (8)
.B list
and
.BR "zfs get" ,
without privileges. It never writes zark's files, takes zark's lock or
imports a pool itself.
.PP
Each operation runs one zark command as
.B pkexec /usr/share/zark/zark
.IR "command ..." ,
under the polkit action of that command
.RI ( /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.juanmitaboada.Zark.policy ),
in a terminal inside the window where zark asks its questions.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Read the files and the live figures again.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Back up the selected drive.
.TP
.B Ctrl+M
Browse the selected drive's files, or unmount it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 ... Ctrl+9
The Overview, then the backup drives in order.
.TP
.B Ctrl+?
The keyboard shortcuts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zark (1)
